:: item.permitAskava [static-storage] {"position":"4300,1925","size":"100,100"}
{=

(metadata: 
	"id", [Askava Entry Permit],
    "key", (a: "document", "legal",),
    "value", (a: 300, 100, 500, 200, 500, 1000,),
    "img", "https://thefifthcity.wiki/w/images/3/3f/Currency3_copper.png",
    "desc", [A piece of paper with your name and a terse description of why you're in Askava, stamped with the magical, tamper-proof seal of the governor.],
    "tip", [This document permits you a one-time passage from Apesai into mainland Askava, collected at either of the 3 major shores: Rokhab, Navveh, or Zirab. Valid once.],
    "gainText", [After some trouble, you are finally granted a permit into Askava.],
    "lossText", [You are loath to part with the precious permit, mostly because it will be bother to get another one if you ever make another trip from the island into the mainland.],
    "content", [{
<!--main content begins-->
''LIGHT BLESSES NURANDAH''
<br>
''Provisional Permission to Travel Into Askava Dahak''<br>Pursuant to article sat-hashtdah-noh of the Immigration and Travel Statute of Askava dahak, year 989.
<br>
<br>
From the Askavan High Court in Apesai and by extension the will and wisdom of Nudankhan,<br>To all immigration and maritime security personnel of the Nurrah rostak,
<br>
<br>
We, DAHAKMAR OF ASKAVA and also BANDAKMAR OF APESAI, hereby grants the holder of this document:

<div style="padding: 1em;">//(print: $char's player's customName), citizen of the Nurandah Empire, magus-in-training, currently journeying under the aegis of their respective institution//</div>

a one-time permission to enter continental Askava via Apesai, in accordance with the declaration of non-immigrantion, non-import, and non-espionage signed in Apesai bandak.
<br>
This document, which under no circumstances can be used as a proof of identity for the holder outside of Askava dahak, is exclusively intended to be used for transit within the dahak, valid for a single journey, to be collected and nullified upon arrival.
<br>
$cssDesc[The document then lists several more disclaimers, waivers, and conditions.]
<br>
<br>
Apesai, (print: $time's year) of the Third Reclaimer,<br>Dahakmar: Dan-Damar-Vehkhan-da-Apesai.
<br>
$cssDesc[There is a blue-wax seal, a sigil depicting an Askavan hare running under the Sun of Nurandah.]
<br>
---
(link: "Put the permit away.")[(goto: $readingNav's before)]
<!--end of content-->

    }],

)